<title>INDIA: India Siemens Apr-Aug sales up 38 pct.</title>
<headline>India Siemens Apr-Aug sales up 38 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The sales of Siemens India rose 38 percent in the first five months of financial year to March 31, 1997, chairman F.A. Mehta said on Friday.  </p>
<p>New orders booked was up 24 percent compared to the year-ago period, he told shareholders at the company's annual general meeting.</p>
<p>Mehta did not give details.</p>
<p>The firm is 51 percent owned by Germany's Siemens AG.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
